payment_retry_reliability::baseline::v2.text:
{
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "C1",
      "statement": "Bank debit mandates are 2.1% of payment attempts but carry 81.8% of failed attempted value ($6,121,598) in 2026-Q2, at an average order value of $1,246.",
      "claim_type": "fact",
      "citations": [
        {"evidence_id": "EV-a7cf8004", "quote": "share_of_attempts_percent: 2.1", "locator": "2026-Q2 bank_debit_mandate row"},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-a7cf8004", "quote": "share_of_failed_value_percent: 81.8", "locator": "2026-Q2 bank_debit_mandate row"},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-a7cf8004", "quote": "failed_attempted_value_usd: 6121598", "locator": "2026-Q2 bank_debit_mandate row"},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-a7cf8004", "quote": "average_order_value_usd: 1246.00", "locator": "2026-Q2 bank_debit_mandate row"}
      ],
      "support_level": "strong",
      "rationale": "Directly measured quarterly metric with an explicit denominator (attempts) and an explicit value basis, owned by analytics and dated 2026-07-15."
    },
    {
      "id": "C2",
      "statement": "Mandate collection success has fallen for four consecutive reported quarters: 90.6% (2025-Q3), 88.1% (2025-Q4), 82.4% (2026-Q1), 71.6% (2026-Q2).",
      "claim_type": "fact",
      "citations": [
        {"evidence_id": "EV-7d84a397", "quote": "success_rate_percent: 90.6", "locator": "2025-Q3 bank_debit_mandate"},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-f0c37296", "quote": "success_rate_percent: 88.1", "locator": "2025-Q4 bank_debit_mandate"},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-a563547e", "quote": "success_rate_percent: 82.4", "locator": "2026-Q1 bank_debit_mandate"},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-a7cf8004", "quote": "success_rate_percent: 71.6", "locator": "2026-Q2 bank_debit_mandate"}
      ],
      "support_level": "strong",
      "rationale": "Four dated rows from the same series. Note the 2026-Q1 denominator change described in EV-367e5a44 applies to the authorisation success series; per-method success rates are computed on attempts, but the reader should confirm with analytics whether the method-level rows were affected."
    },
    {
      "id": "C3",
      "statement": "By count, cards are the majority of failed payment attempts: 19,369 of 25,908 in 2026-Q2.",
      "claim_type": "fact",
      "citations": [
        {"evidence_id": "EV-5219cbf8", "quote": "Cards account for 19,369 of the 25,908 failed authorisation attempts in 2026-Q2."}
      ],
      "support_level": "strong",
      "rationale": "Counts reconcile with the failed_authorisation_count metric of 25,908."
    },
    {
      "id": "C4",
      "statement": "The Retry Orchestrator is measurably degraded: retries issued per eligible failure fell from 3.1 (2025-Q4) to 1.3 (2026-Q2) against a designed policy of up to four, and card retry recovery fell from 41.8% to 34.2%.",
      "claim_type": "fact",
      "citations": [
        {"evidence_id": "EV-d4e10def", "quote": "value: 1.3", "locator": "2026-Q2 retries_per_eligible_failure"},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-1326a5ac", "quote": "value: 3.1", "locator": "2025-Q4 retries_per_eligible_failure"},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-0fa7ef7a", "quote": "value: 41.8", "locator": "2026-Q1 retry_recovery_rate, card_methods_only"},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-bd7f4e82", "quote": "value: 34.2", "locator": "2026-Q2 retry_recovery_rate, card_methods_only"}
      ],
      "support_level": "strong",
      "rationale": "Dated analytics series corroborated by the incident review."
    },
    {
      "id": "C5",
      "statement": "The cause of the retry drops is a hypothesis, not an established finding, and the defect has never been reproduced outside production.",
      "claim_type": "assumption",
      "citations": [
        {"evidence_id": "EV-5219cbf8", "quote": "The leading hypothesis is queue lease expiry: a retry job whose 15-minute lease expires before a worker collects it is dropped, and the drop emits no alert. This is consistent with the burst pattern and with the load profile, but it has not been demonstrated."},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-5219cbf8", "quote": "The defect has not been reproduced outside production."}
      ],
      "support_level": "moderate",
      "rationale": "The incident review is explicit that the mechanism is suspected. Three of eleven bursts also coincided with partner-reported degradation, so an issuer-side contribution is not fully excluded."
    },
    {
      "id": "C6",
      "statement": "PT-2026-014 is an open High-severity finding inside the cardholder data environment with a contractual remediation deadline of 2026-09-15, and the assessor has not retested it.",
      "claim_type": "governance_constraint",
      "citations": [
        {"evidence_id": "EV-9e2b26eb", "quote": "\"severity\": \"High\""},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-9e2b26eb", "quote": "\"remediation_deadline\": \"2026-09-15\""},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-9e2b26eb", "quote": "\"retested_by_assessor\": false"},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-9e2b26eb", "quote": "The retry queue payload is unchanged and 30 days of historical log entries were still in retention at the date of this register."}
      ],
      "support_level": "strong",
      "rationale": "Security-owned register dated 2026-07-24."
    },
    {
      "id": "C7",
      "statement": "Remediation of a contractually-deadlined finding is not a backlog candidate and may not be scored or traded against product work; only assessor retest closes it.",
      "claim_type": "governance_constraint",
      "citations": [
        {"evidence_id": "EV-0089742e", "quote": "Remediation of a finding with a contractual deadline is a compliance obligation, not a candidate initiative."},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-0089742e", "quote": "A finding may be recorded as remediated only when the assessor has retested it."}
      ],
      "support_level": "strong",
      "rationale": "Explicit policy text owned by risk-and-compliance, updated 2026-06-05."
    },
    {
      "id": "C8",
      "statement": "Only one change to a given in-scope component may be in flight at a time, with a ten business day change-control lead time, so any orchestrator product change queues behind the remediation.",
      "claim_type": "governance_constraint",
      "citations": [
        {"evidence_id": "EV-0089742e", "quote": "Any change to a component inside the cardholder data environment requires a change-control review with a ten business day lead time, and only one change to a given in-scope component may be in flight at a time."},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-0e4c2c0a", "quote": "Only one change to the orchestrator can be in flight under change control. Whatever else we choose, it queues behind the remediation."}
      ],
      "support_level": "strong",
      "rationale": "Policy text plus engineering manager confirmation. The second citation is an opinion in form but restates the policy."
    },
    {
      "id": "C9",
      "statement": "No failure-reason breakdown exists for mandate collections because the scheme return file reason codes are stored as raw strings and never parsed.",
      "claim_type": "technical_constraint",
      "citations": [
        {"evidence_id": "EV-367e5a44", "quote": "Its reason codes are stored as raw strings and are not parsed, so no failure-reason breakdown exists for mandate collections."},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-7083aa45", "quote": "Reason codes were read by hand from the scheme return file because they are not parsed by any system."}
      ],
      "support_level": "strong",
      "rationale": "Stated independently by engineering and by the experiment record."
    },
    {
      "id": "C10",
      "statement": "The only evidence on why mandates fail is a hand review of 60 collections from a single weekly batch and a single onboarding cohort; it is not a population estimate and has never been reproduced.",
      "claim_type": "fact",
      "citations": [
        {"evidence_id": "EV-7083aa45", "quote": "A manual review of 60 failed mandate collections from a single week found: 22 recorded as mandate no longer valid at the buyer's bank, 19 as insufficient funds, 11 as account closed, and 8 unmapped."},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-7083aa45", "quote": "All 60 came from one weekly batch and from buyers onboarded in the same quarter."},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-7083aa45", "quote": "No follow-up review has been run and the finding has not been reproduced at scale."}
      ],
      "support_level": "low",
      "rationale": "n=60, self-selected by batch and cohort, against roughly 4,913 failed mandate collections implied by the 2026-Q2 row. Percentages from it are not facts about the mandate population."
    },
    {
      "id": "C11",
      "statement": "The vendor's claimed 2.4 percentage point authorisation uplift is an unqualified vendor figure with no baseline, sample, method or merchant category.",
      "claim_type": "stakeholder_opinion",
      "citations": [
        {"evidence_id": "EV-0e4c2c0a", "quote": "A vendor product circulated by the Director of Payments claims a 2.4 percentage point uplift in authorisation success."},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-0e4c2c0a", "quote": "The material states no baseline, no sample size, no comparison method, and no merchant category. No independent evaluation was provided."}
      ],
      "support_level": "low",
      "rationale": "A number with no denominator or method is an opinion about a number."
    },
    {
      "id": "C12",
      "statement": "Acceptance cost is the binding financial constraint; any proposal that raises blended acceptance cost needs finance approval before a pilot, and the cost index has already risen from 99.1 to 100.0 quarter on quarter.",
      "claim_type": "business_constraint",
      "citations": [
        {"evidence_id": "EV-3cc53aed", "quote": "The cost of payment acceptance is the binding financial constraint. Any proposal that raises the blended acceptance cost requires finance approval before a pilot may begin."},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-94934b9a", "quote": "value: 99.1", "locator": "2026-Q1 payment_acceptance_cost_index"},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-70c4b59a", "quote": "value: 100.0", "locator": "2026-Q2 payment_acceptance_cost_index"}
      ],
      "support_level": "strong",
      "rationale": "Strategy document plus two dated index readings. The index is unitless; no absolute cost figure is available."
    },
    {
      "id": "C13",
      "statement": "The February 2026 decision not to invest in mandate work was justified on share of attempts (~2%), a denominator that excludes the value dimension on which mandates dominate.",
      "claim_type": "business_constraint",
      "citations": [
        {"evidence_id": "EV-b2ce4516", "quote": "bank mandates are around two per cent of payment attempts, which does not justify engineering investment this year."},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-a7cf8004", "quote": "share_of_failed_value_percent: 81.8", "locator": "2026-Q2 bank_debit_mandate row"}
      ],
      "support_level": "strong",
      "rationale": "Both statements are accurate on their own denominators; the prior decision predates the 2026-Q2 data and the fall to 71.6%."
    },
    {
      "id": "C14",
      "statement": "Direct debit scheme rules cap re-presentations at two, require three business days between them, require buyer notification three working days ahead, and require certification before any change to collection retry frequency.",
      "claim_type": "governance_constraint",
      "citations": [
        {"evidence_id": "EV-0089742e", "quote": "A failed mandate collection may be re-presented no more than twice."},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-0089742e", "quote": "Re-presentations must be at least three business days apart, and the buyer must be notified at least three working days before each one."},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-0089742e", "quote": "Any change to collection retry frequency must be certified against the scheme rules before it is enabled."}
      ],
      "support_level": "strong",
      "rationale": "Policy text; caps the upside of any mandate retry-frequency intervention."
    },
    {
      "id": "C15",
      "statement": "A message recommending a different payment method is classified as marketing and requires recorded consent, whereas a plain failure notice does not.",
      "claim_type": "governance_constraint",
      "citations": [
        {"evidence_id": "EV-0089742e", "quote": "A message that recommends a different payment method is classified as marketing under the current policy and requires recorded marketing consent from that buyer."},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-0089742e", "quote": "A notice telling a buyer that a payment failed is transactional and does not require consent."}
      ],
      "support_level": "strong",
      "rationale": "Directly constrains any fallback-prompt design; the addressable audience shrinks to consented buyers, a count nobody has produced."
    },
    {
      "id": "C16",
      "statement": "No payments change may be deployed between 2026-11-10 and 2027-01-05, and discretionary product work is not exempt.",
      "claim_type": "governance_constraint",
      "citations": [
        {"evidence_id": "EV-0089742e", "quote": "No payments change may be deployed between 2026-11-10 and 2027-01-05. Security remediation with a contractual deadline is exempt from the freeze; discretionary product work is not."}
      ],
      "support_level": "strong",
      "rationale": "Compresses the delivery window for any option chosen now."
    },
    {
      "id": "C17",
      "statement": "Trade buyer GMV is a stated FY26 growth priority, and mandates are used almost entirely by trade and wholesale buyers.",
      "claim_type": "business_constraint",
      "citations": [
        {"evidence_id": "EV-3cc53aed", "quote": "Gross merchandise value from trade buyers is a stated growth priority for FY26."},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-a7cf8004", "quote": "note: used almost entirely by trade and wholesale buyers - synthetic", "locator": "2026-Q2 bank_debit_mandate row"}
      ],
      "support_level": "strong",
      "rationale": "Links the failing method to the segment the business says it wants to grow."
    },
    {
      "id": "C18",
      "statement": "The authorisation success series is not comparable across 2026-Q1: the denominator changed and raised the reported rate by about 0.9 points, and the earlier series has never been restated.",
      "claim_type": "technical_constraint",
      "citations": [
        {"evidence_id": "EV-367e5a44", "quote": "From 2026-Q1 the authorisation success denominator excludes checkout sessions abandoned by the buyer before the issuer responded. The change raised the reported rate by approximately 0.9 percentage points."},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-2b90214e", "quote": "note: not restated - the pre-2026-Q1 series has never been recomputed on the current denominator - synthetic"}
      ],
      "support_level": "strong",
      "rationale": "Means the FY26 target of 98.0% and the current 96.9% sit on different bases from the historic series; on a like-for-like basis the underlying rate may be roughly 0.9 points lower than pre-2026 figures suggest."
    },
    {
      "id": "C19",
      "statement": "Blended authorisation success was 96.9% in 2026-Q2 against a contractual floor of 96.0%, having declined from 97.2% (2025-Q4) and 97.0% (2026-Q1).",
      "claim_type": "fact",
      "citations": [
        {"evidence_id": "EV-b0554146", "quote": "value: 96.9", "locator": "2026-Q2 authorisation_success_rate, all_methods"},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-c4ea234c", "quote": "value: 97.0", "locator": "2026-Q1 authorisation_success_rate, all_methods"},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-3cc53aed", "quote": "The partner agreement warrants a quarterly authorisation success rate of not less than 96.0% measured across all payment methods."}
      ],
      "support_level": "moderate",
      "rationale": "The 2026-Q2 and 2026-Q1 readings are on the revised denominator; the 97.2% 2025-Q4 reading is on the old basis and should not be trended directly against them (see C18)."
    },
    {
      "id": "C20",
      "statement": "Nobody knows how much failed value is recovered when a buyer returns by another route: the field exists and was never populated.",
      "claim_type": "fact",
      "citations": [
        {"evidence_id": "EV-c8aafb0e", "quote": "note: not measured - the field exists but was never populated - synthetic", "locator": "2026-Q2 orders_recovered_after_payment_failure"},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-5219cbf8", "quote": "No estimate exists of how much of the failed value is eventually recovered when a buyer whose payment failed returns and completes the order by another route."}
      ],
      "support_level": "strong",
      "rationale": "Blank is not zero. Every financial-impact figure in this brief is an upper bound on recoverable value until this is populated."
    },
    {
      "id": "C21",
      "statement": "The only randomised payment reliability test run to date moved the second card retry to four hours and lifted card retry recovery from 39.1% to 41.6% over 24,800 eligible failures (p=0.03); it covered card methods only.",
      "claim_type": "fact",
      "citations": [
        {"evidence_id": "EV-7083aa45", "quote": "Card retry recovery was 41.6% in the treatment arm against 39.1% in the control arm, over 24,800 eligible failures. The difference is statistically significant at p = 0.03."},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-7083aa45", "quote": "The test covered card methods only. Bank mandate collections were excluded because they are not routed through the Retry Orchestrator."}
      ],
      "support_level": "strong",
      "rationale": "Randomised, adequately powered, and explicitly scoped. A 2.5 point recovery gain on cards is the realistic order of magnitude for retry tuning — well below the vendor's unqualified 2.4 point claim on overall authorisation success."
    },
    {
      "id": "C22",
      "statement": "The trade sales view that 'the bank transfer thing is broken' is an unquantified recollection; no buyer count, frequency or period was available.",
      "claim_type": "stakeholder_opinion",
      "citations": [
        {"evidence_id": "EV-0e4c2c0a", "quote": "Our trade buyers keep telling me the bank transfer thing is broken. I hear it every week."},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-0e4c2c0a", "quote": "Asked how many buyers, how often, and over what period, no figure was available."}
      ],
      "support_level": "low",
      "rationale": "Directionally consistent with the mandate metrics, but it is testimony, not measurement, and should not be cited as sizing."
    },
    {
      "id": "C23",
      "statement": "Retry recovery is not measured at all for mandate collections, because they are not routed through the orchestrator.",
      "claim_type": "fact",
      "citations": [
        {"evidence_id": "EV-2e1dc93f", "quote": "note: not measured - mandate collections are not routed through the orchestrator - synthetic", "locator": "2026-Q2 retry_recovery_rate, bank_debit_mandate"},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-367e5a44", "quote": "Mandate collections are assembled in a nightly batch and submitted to the scheme directly. They do not pass through the Retry Orchestrator, and no change to orchestrator retry policy affects them."}
      ],
      "support_level": "strong",
      "rationale": "Decisive for scoping: no orchestrator or adaptive-retry intervention touches the 81.8% of failed value carried by mandates."
    },
    {
      "id": "C24",
      "statement": "Extending the retry lease requires an unscheduled broker upgrade, and retry behaviour cannot be validated before release because no non-production environment carries live issuer traffic and shadow traffic is unsupported.",
      "claim_type": "technical_constraint",
      "citations": [
        {"evidence_id": "EV-367e5a44", "quote": "A job whose lease expires before a worker collects it is dropped, and the drop is not alerted. Extending the lease requires a broker upgrade that is not scheduled."},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-367e5a44", "quote": "Changes to retry behaviour cannot be validated before release except by shadow traffic, which the orchestrator does not currently support."}
      ],
      "support_level": "strong",
      "rationale": "Raises both effort and release risk for any orchestrator-side option."
    }
  ],
  "contradictions": [
    {
      "id": "CON1",
      "topic": "Whether PT-2026-014 is effectively closed",
      "kind": "claim_conflict",
      "side_a": {"evidence_id": "EV-367e5a44", "quote": "The identifier no longer appears in application logs, so from an engineering standpoint the exposure described in PT-2026-014 was closed on 2026-06-12."},
      "side_b": {"evidence_id": "EV-0e4c2c0a", "quote": "The finding is open. The queue payload still carries the identifier and 84 engineers can read the logs."},
      "summary": "Engineering treats the 2026-06-12 logging change as closing the exposure; the security lead says the queue payload and log access are unchanged. The register records the finding as open, not retested, with the retry queue payload unchanged.",
      "how_to_resolve": "Only assessor retest settles it: governance states a finding may be recorded as remediated only when the assessor has retested it. Ask security for the retest booking date against the 2026-09-15 deadline and confirm whether the queue payload change is in scope of the retest."
    },
    {
      "id": "CON2",
      "topic": "What is the 'largest' payment failure problem",
      "kind": "scope_conflict",
      "side_a": {"evidence_id": "EV-5219cbf8", "quote": "Cards account for 19,369 of the 25,908 failed authorisation attempts in 2026-Q2."},
      "side_b": {"evidence_id": "EV-a7cf8004", "quote": "share_of_failed_value_percent: 81.8", "locator": "2026-Q2 bank_debit_mandate row"},
      "summary": "Both are true of different segments and different denominators. Cards are the largest failure population by count (consumer-weighted, low AOV). Mandates are the largest failure population by value (trade-weighted, $1,246 AOV). Choosing between count and value implicitly chooses between consumer and trade buyers.",
      "how_to_resolve": "Agree with the steering group which denominator the FY26 goals are scored on. The backlog currently scores on 'customer reach, revenue impact, and engineering effort', which pulls in opposite directions here; a written tie-break rule would settle it."
    },
    {
      "id": "CON3",
      "topic": "Headline authorisation success rate",
      "kind": "temporal_conflict",
      "side_a": {"evidence_id": "EV-3cc53aed", "quote": "Payment authorisation success is 97.4% and has been stable for six quarters."},
      "side_b": {"evidence_id": "EV-b0554146", "quote": "value: 96.9", "locator": "2026-Q2 authorisation_success_rate, all_methods"},
      "summary": "The strategy document's 97.4% is stale, not wrong: it matches the 2025-Q3 and 2025-Q2 rows of the metric series and was written on 2026-02-10. The current reading is 96.9% for 2026-Q2, on a denominator that was changed in 2026-Q1 and raised the reported rate by about 0.9 points.",
      "how_to_resolve": "Have analytics restate the pre-2026-Q1 series on the current denominator, then reset the FY26 98.0% target to the same basis. Until then no trend statement spanning 2026-Q1 is safe."
    },
    {
      "id": "CON4",
      "topic": "Whether the pen-test fix should be ranked on the product backlog",
      "kind": "claim_conflict",
      "side_a": {"evidence_id": "EV-0e4c2c0a", "quote": "Put the pen-test fix on the same backlog as everything else and let the scores decide. If it wins, it wins."},
      "side_b": {"evidence_id": "EV-0089742e", "quote": "Remediation of a finding with a contractual deadline is a compliance obligation, not a candidate initiative."},
      "summary": "The Director of Payments wants the remediation scored against product work; the governance policy forbids it. This is an executive preference against a written obligation, not two competing readings of evidence.",
      "how_to_resolve": "Risk-and-compliance owns the policy and should confirm in writing to the steering group that PT-2026-014 is scheduled against 2026-09-15 outside the ranked backlog. Note also the commercial view that it is 'a paperwork item' does not change the contractual deadline."
    },
    {
      "id": "CON5",
      "topic": "Whether mandate work is worth engineering investment",
      "kind": "scope_conflict",
      "side_a": {"evidence_id": "EV-b2ce4516", "quote": "bank mandates are around two per cent of payment attempts, which does not justify engineering investment this year."},
      "side_b": {"evidence_id": "EV-a7cf8004", "quote": "failed_attempted_value_usd: 6121598", "locator": "2026-Q2 bank_debit_mandate row"},
      "summary": "D-2026-02 (2026-02-27) is arithmetically correct on share of attempts and silent on share of failed value. It also predates the fall in mandate success from 82.4% in 2026-Q1 to 71.6% in 2026-Q2.",
      "how_to_resolve": "Re-table D-2026-02 at the monthly steering review with the 2026-Q2 value-weighted data and the mandate success trend. The decision should be explicitly reaffirmed or reversed rather than left as an unexamined precedent."
    }
  ],
  "missing_evidence": [
    {
      "id": "ME1",
      "question": "What is the population-level failure-reason breakdown for mandate collections?",
      "impact": "would_change_recommendation",
      "why_it_matters": "The entire mandate case rests on a hand review of 60 records from one weekly batch and one onboarding cohort. If failures are dominated by insufficient funds, re-validation is the wrong remedy; if by invalid or closed mandates, it is the right one. The two point to different interventions with different costs.",
      "how_to_obtain": "Parse the nightly scheme return file reason codes into the warehouse and report a full-quarter breakdown by reason, by buyer tenure, and by value. This is the recommended option itself.",
      "was_searched": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ME2",
      "question": "How many orders are recovered after a payment failure by another route, and at what value?",
      "impact": "would_change_support_level",
      "why_it_matters": "The field exists and was never populated, and the incident review says no estimate exists. Every 'failed value' figure quoted here is therefore an upper bound on recoverable value, potentially by a large margin. It was asked in the stakeholder review and nobody had the number.",
      "how_to_obtain": "Join failed authorisation events to subsequent successful orders from the same buyer within a defined window in the warehouse; populate the existing metric field for at least two back-quarters.",
      "was_searched": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ME3",
      "question": "What does any of these options cost in engineering effort or money?",
      "impact": "would_change_recommendation",
      "why_it_matters": "No effort estimate, sprint cost, headcount figure or vendor price appears anywhere in the evidence, yet the backlog is scored partly on engineering effort. Every 'delivery_effort' and 'spend' assessment in this brief is therefore either unassessable or inferred from constraints rather than from an estimate.",
      "how_to_obtain": "Ask engineering for a t-shirt estimate on each option and ask finance for the vendor per-transaction fee restated against the current acceptance cost index.",
      "was_searched": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ME4",
      "question": "How many distinct trade buyers are affected by mandate failures, and is failed value concentrated in a few accounts?",
      "impact": "would_refine_scope",
      "why_it_matters": "At $1,246 average order value, a handful of large accounts could account for most of the $6.1m. That would make account-level manual outreach a cheaper remedy than any platform change. The Head of Trade Sales could not supply a buyer count.",
      "how_to_obtain": "Warehouse query: distinct buyers with a failed mandate collection in 2026-Q2, with value concentration (top-10 share).",
      "was_searched": true
    },
    {
      "id": "ME5",
